    <briefdescription>
<para>Stores a preprocessor &apos;<ref refid="matcherparser_8C_1a709183e322e370a05cfdd3bb79f9ae79" kindref="member">if</ref>&apos; directive and nested directives. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classCPreproc_1_1If" kindref="compound">If</ref> represents one instance of a preprocessor &apos;<ref refid="matcherparser_8C_1a709183e322e370a05cfdd3bb79f9ae79" kindref="member">if</ref>&apos; directive, including all its cases. That is, a <ref refid="classCPreproc_1_1If" kindref="compound">If</ref> object corresponding to the following &apos;<ref refid="matcherparser_8C_1a709183e322e370a05cfdd3bb79f9ae79" kindref="member">if</ref>&apos; directive,</para><para><ref refid="matcherparser_8C_1a709183e322e370a05cfdd3bb79f9ae79" kindref="member">if</ref> C_1 ... #elif C_2 ... #elif C_k ... #endif // k+1</para><para>stores a sequence of k cases plus the final &apos;#endif&apos;. One may view a <ref refid="classCPreproc_1_1If" kindref="compound">If</ref> object as a container of cases (If::Cases).</para><para>In addition, <ref refid="classCPreproc_1_1If" kindref="compound">If</ref> represents the complete tree of nested &apos;<ref refid="matcherparser_8C_1a709183e322e370a05cfdd3bb79f9ae79" kindref="member">if</ref>&apos; directives. See the case object, <ref refid="classCPreproc_1_1If_1_1Case" kindref="compound">If::Case</ref>, for more information. </para>    </detaileddescription>
